Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "FoggyUrbanDriving" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :vehicle1, :vehicle2, :vehicle3 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :fog1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Black vehicle parked on the right" .
:vehicle2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Yellow vehicle parked ahead" .
:vehicle3 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Distant vehicle in opposing lane" .

:fog1 a :FoggyCondition .

:risk1 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Visibility significantly reduced by dense fog" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .
:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:risk2 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of collision with parked vehicles or lane drift due to low visibility" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .
:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.65"^^xsd:float .

Identified Risks for each risk class
Risk 1:
Description: Occlusion risk caused by dense fog severely limiting the sensor range and visibility of the driving environment.
Severity Score: 0.75

Risk 2:
Description: Lane intrusion risk due to reduced situational awareness and potential proximity to parked vehicles at the edge of the lane in low visibility.
Severity Score: 0.65